                <pb facs="0272" n="188" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg188"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Beaupré to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-08-24"><hi rendition="#italic">August 24, 1903</hi></date>.
                        (Received 28.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>August 24, 11 a.m. Nothing has been done, and very little satisfactory action,
                    this depending upon the attitude of the Government of the United States, which
                    is waited for in great anxiety. The report of the committee prepared. Have
                    received telegram of 13th; none later.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaupré.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
